KNOWNBUG
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
no body for callee
--
The CPROVER library has no model for any of the <wchar.h> wide-character
array and string functions (wmemcpy, wmemmove, wmemset, wmemcmp, wmemchr,
wcslen, ...): calls to them are "no body for callee" and return or write
nondeterministic values.  libstdc++'s char_traits<wchar_t> uses them, so
std::char_traits<wchar_t>::copy and std::wstring operations are
nondeterministic.  gcc runs this program without assertion failure.
